Can I use MINE with existing View-based UI? <p>Yes, while MINE is Compose-first, you can wrap composables in ComposeView:</p> <pre><code>val composeView = ComposeView(context).apply {
    setContent {
        IndoorNavigationScene(mapBuild)
    }
}
viewGroup.addView(composeView)
</code></pre> Does MINE support AR features? <p>MINE focuses on indoor navigation. For AR, you can integrate ARCore separately and use SceneView's AR capabilities alongside MINE's navigation logic.</p> What's the minimum Android version? <p>Android 7.0 (API 24) for basic functionality. Some features like Vulkan backend require API 28+.</p> How do I update maps without app releases? <p>Use <code>MapLoader.loadFromUrl()</code> to fetch maps from your CDN:</p> <pre><code>val mapBuild = MapLoader.loadFromUrl(
    "https://cdn.example.com/venues/${venueId}.json"
)
</code></pre>

